# Everything under `api/` becomes a serverless function under zero-config
# detection. A test file left there deploys as a PUBLIC endpoint — `/api/x.test`
# — and drags its devDependencies (vitest) into the bundle. Excluded here as
# well as moved out of `api/`, so a test file dropped into `api/` later still
# cannot become a route.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
**/*.spec.ts
**/*.spec.tsx

# Fixtures and harnesses that only tests import.
#
# `**/test/` AND NOT JUST `server/test/`, because the narrow form broke the
# build the first time a second test directory appeared. The patterns above
# match a FILENAME (`*.test.ts`); a harness is called `harness.ts`, so
# `server/shop/cart/test/harness.ts` matched nothing, shipped, and then imported
# `../../../test/harness` — a path this file had excluded. Result: `tsc -b`
# passed locally, where `server/test/` exists, and failed the deploy with
# TS2307 on a module no production code references. Excluding the directory by
# name keeps the two halves consistent however many of them there are.
**/test/
server/test/
